        <div class="plate__copy">
          <h2 class="plate__pair">
          <span class="plate__word">Block.</span>
          <span class="plate__word plate__word--accent" data-accent="yellow">Brace.</span>
          <span class="plate__word">Lash.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="plate__story" data-reveal>
            <p>Inside a container the cargo has nowhere to go but into the walls. Timber blocking, bracing frames and lashings have to hold through road, rail and sea, and how they are fitted is the whole difference between cargo that arrives and cargo that shifts. A loading and stowage survey documents the securing as fitted, with the container number, the seal and photographs, before the doors close.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="plate__meta">Cylindrical units braced inside a container · AI-generated illustration based on a photograph from Nick’s files</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

